Description:The present invention provides a Prefabricated Spaceframe based Modular Structure for buildings that can be easily erected at the site. A plurality of the modular units can be joined together to expand the design by forming a building with a larger space and capacity. The modular units can be packaged with matching sizes of panels of walls, floors, and roofs made from suitable materials to comply to architectural and comfort requirements, besides being environment friendly. The said panels can be pre-assembled over the spaceframes, or assembled at the site. The spaceframes or completed modular units can be fabricated at a factory or remote location and easily transported to the site thus saving time and cost. The modules and buildings so made are relocatable. 
Ref. Drawing: Fig 1 , Claims:CLAIMS
WE CLAIM:
1. A Prefabricated Spaceframe Based Modular Building Structure 1 that is capable of easy relocation, comprising: 
a plurality of Unit Modules 2, each comprising of vertical Main Members 3; 
Horizontal Members 4; 
Portal Brackets 5;
Corner Brackets 6; 
Floor Modules 8 and 9, and; 
Diagonal Module 39
2. A Prefabricated Spaceframe Based Modular Building Structure as in claim 1 wherein the Main Members 3, Horizontal Members 4 and Diagonal Members 39 are made of identical cross-section of Hollow Square Tube of pre-designed sectional area, thickness and length of members based on perceived size of building module, that renders an innovative method of joining them with Portal and Corner Brackets 5 and 6.
3. A Prefabricated Spaceframe Based Modular Building Structure as in claim 1 wherein the Unit Module 2 can be joined periodically in all the three dimensions to obtain a Building in length and breadth in multiples of Unit Module and also a multi-storey configuration.
4. A Prefabricated Spaceframe Based Modular Building Structure as in claim 1 wherein because of Modularity the Building Structure can be added with new Unit Modules or relocated easily.
5. A Prefabricated Spaceframe Based Modular Building Structure as in claim 1 wherein additional strengthening and rigidity can be added by using Diagonal Members at some Unit Modules if required. 
6. A method of placement and precise location of each prefabricated building module on site using laser projection

