 , Claims:WE CLAIM:
1. A bio-responsive wound dressing with integrated microchip sensing 100 comprising of
cellulose-based hydrogel matrix 102 to provide a biocompatible and moisture-retentive dressing environment for wound care; 
miniaturized microchips 104 to enable data processing and integration with biosensors; 
ph sensor 106 to monitor acidity or alkalinity levels in the wound environment; 
temperature sensor 108 to track changes in wound temperature for infection detection; 
wireless communication module 110 to transmit real-time data to external devices; 
biocompatible power source 112 to provide continuous energy for sensors and communication; 
mobile application 114 to display wound data and provide remote monitoring; and
alert system 116 to notify healthcare providers of critical wound conditions promptly.

2. The bio-responsive wound dressing with integrated microchip sensing 100, wherein the cellulose-based hydrogel matrix 102 is configured to provide a biocompatible, moisture-retentive environment for wound healing and secure integration of embedded electronic components.

3. The bio-responsive wound dressing with integrated microchip sensing 100 as claimed in claim 1, wherein miniaturized microchips 104 are configured to process data from biosensors and transmit real-time information through wireless communication for continuous monitoring.

4. The bio-responsive wound dressing with integrated microchip sensing 100 as claimed in claim 1, wherein ph sensor 106 is configured to detect changes in the wound environment’s acidity or alkalinity to identify potential risks of infection.

5. The bio-responsive wound dressing with integrated microchip sensing 100 as claimed in claim 1, wherein temperature sensor 108 is configured to monitor variations in wound temperature for early detection of inflammatory conditions or infections.

6. The bio-responsive wound dressing with integrated microchip sensing 100 as claimed in claim 1, wherein wireless communication module 110 is configured to transmit biomarker data from the embedded microchips to a mobile application, enabling remote healthcare monitoring.

7. The bio-responsive wound dressing with integrated microchip sensing 100 as claimed in claim 1, wherein the miniaturized microchips 104, ph sensor 106, temperature sensor 108, wireless communication module 110, and biocompatible power source 112 are configured to collectively enable real-time monitoring of wound biomarkers by processing data within the hydrogel matrix 102, transmitting the data to a mobile application 114 for remote visualization, and triggering alerts via the alert system 116 when biomarker thresholds indicate potential complications, ensuring seamless integration and uninterrupted functionality for advanced wound care.

8. The bio-responsive wound dressing with integrated microchip sensing 100 as claimed in claim 1, wherein mobile application 114 is configured to display real-time wound condition data and send alerts based on predefined critical thresholds for timely medical intervention.

9. The bio-responsive wound dressing with integrated microchip sensing 100 as claimed in claim 1, wherein alert system 116 is configured to notify healthcare providers immediately when biomarker readings indicate critical wound conditions, enabling prompt medical response.

10. The bio-responsive wound dressing with integrated microchip sensing 100 as claimed in claim 1, wherein method comprises of 

preparing the cellulose-based hydrogel matrix 102 by integrating miniaturized microchips 104 during the gelation process to ensure secure and seamless placement;
functionalizing the ph sensor 106 and temperature sensor 108 embedded in the hydrogel matrix 102 to enable the detection of wound biomarkers;
continuously monitoring critical wound conditions, such as ph levels and temperature, to detect healing progress or signs of infection using sensors 106 and 108;
transmitting real-time data from the miniaturized microchips 104 via the wireless communication module 110 to the mobile application 114;
displaying the wound data, including ph and temperature trends, on the mobile application 114 for healthcare providers to monitor remotely;
providing continuous energy to the sensors 106 and 108, the miniaturized microchips 104, and the wireless communication module 110 using the biocompatible power source 112 to ensure uninterrupted functionality;
triggering notifications via the alert system 116 integrated with the mobile application 114 when biomarker readings from the sensors 106 and 108 exceed critical thresholds, enabling timely medical intervention.
